; DNSSEC_INSECURE_ISLAND.
;
; This zone is unsigned and test.zone delegates to it with no DS record. The
; parent is signed, so a validating resolver proves the *absence* of a DS via
; NSEC/NSEC3 and correctly treats this subtree as insecure: AD=0, resolves fine,
; NOT bogus.
;
; The distinction matters commercially. "Insecure" is a warning a customer can
; ignore; "bogus" means validating resolvers see nothing and their mail is
; already broken. Reporting one as the other is exactly the false alarm that
; makes a monitoring product worse than not existing.
$ORIGIN insecure-island.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.

@       IN TXT  "unsigned-but-valid"
_dmarc  IN TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@insecure-island.test"
